.TH GIT-LOCALBRANCHTIDY 1 "2026-09-07" "git-localbranchtidy 0.1.1" "Git Extensions"
.SH NAME
git-localbranchtidy \- delete local branches already merged into the main branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git localbranchtidy
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git localbranchtidy
detects the repository's main branch (usually
.B main
or
.BR master )
and deletes every local branch whose tip is reachable from it, i.e. every
branch that has already been merged.
.PP
The main branch and the currently checked\-out branch are always left
alone. Branches are removed with
.RB \[dq] "git branch \-d" \[dq],
so a branch that is not actually merged is never deleted even if it is
listed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Ask for confirmation before removing each branch. Any answer other than
.B y
or
.B yes
(case\-insensitive) leaves the branch in place. End of input is treated as
a declined prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-main\-branch " NAME"
Use
.I NAME
as the main branch instead of auto\-detecting it. The named branch must
exist locally.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH "MAIN BRANCH DETECTION"
When
.B \-\-main\-branch
is not given, the main branch is resolved in this order:
.IP 1. 4
.BR origin/HEAD ,
the default branch reported by the remote, when the corresponding local
branch exists.
.IP 2. 4
A local branch named
.BR main .
.IP 3. 4
A local branch named
.BR master .
.PP
If none of these apply the command exits with an error asking for
.BR \-\-main\-branch .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success, including the case where there were no merged branches to
remove.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: the main branch could not be detected, an option was
misused, or a
.B git
command failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Tidy up after merging some feature branches:
.EX
git localbranchtidy
.EE
.TP
Review each deletion first:
.EX
git localbranchtidy \-\-interactive
.EE
.TP
Treat
.B trunk
as the main branch:
.EX
git localbranchtidy \-\-main\-branch trunk
.EE
.SH NOTES
Detection relies on the branch tip being an ancestor of the main branch.
Branches that were squash\-merged or rebase\-merged do not appear as merged
and are therefore not removed.
.PP
Because git rewrites
.RB \[dq] "git localbranchtidy \-\-help" \[dq]
into a request for this manual page, use
.RB \[dq] "git localbranchtidy \-h" \[dq]
to see the inline usage summary.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR git-branch (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Graham Ollis.
